import csv,json
from pathlib import Path
b=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
q=list(csv.DictReader((b/'queue.csv').open()));cl=json.loads((b/'lead-clocks.json').read_text());gg=json.loads((b/'lead-gaia-covariance.json').read_text());aa=json.loads((b/'lead-alias-covered-windows.json').read_text())
notes={
'150606032':('P','BYCATCH_GAIA_INCONSISTENT','Broad bounded shallow eclipses recur in raw SAP at approximately18.68458 d, with another eclipse kind near phase0.39. Independent target-centered extraction recovers the S7 event. This clock is incompatible with Gaia27.42594 d. The long-baseline timing residuals reach0.0184d and several small-integer alternatives remain noise limited.','Shallow variable baseline, unresolved capable neighbor capacity, and imperfect eclipse clock prevent confirmation.','Resolve neighbors and measure a new eclipse and both eclipse kinds.'),
'157000271':('REFUTED','OFF_TARGET_CONTAMINATION','Real narrow eclipses at1495.63888,1513.27205,2218.45869 and2236.09264 BTJD follow17.629745 d. Independent difference images in S7 and S33 place their deficit on the bright northern star several pixels from the target. This is positive off-target evidence, not merely an uncertain centroid.','The contaminating eclipsing source is not identified here. The aperture clock is not a period of the selected Gaia source.','Identify and review the northern contaminant separately.'),
'192831602':('P','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_CONSISTENT','Four narrow bounded approximately9ppt eclipses span S5,S6,S32,S87. Consecutive early events and later repeats recover39.167170 d. Gaia39.144337 plus/minus0.044364 d and source-specific conjunctions agree within propagated covariance. Custom extraction and difference image recover the event at target position.','Close-neighbor capacity must be resolved to confirm ownership; independent extraction reuses the same photons.','Resolve capable neighbors and obtain additional eclipse or RV measurements.'),
'198590540':('REFUTED','OFF_TARGET_CONTAMINATION','A strong8.933048 d deep-event clock, with alternating shallow events, is real in QLP across eight sectors. The independent S80 difference image places the eclipse deficit at a bright source approximately2.46 pixels from the target, while target3x3 loss is only about17ppt versus hundreds of ppt in QLP. Selected-target eclipses are refuted.','Contaminant identity and its novelty are unassigned. These are aperture-signal measurements only.','Identify the bright neighboring eclipsing source separately.'),
'218292999':('P','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_CONSISTENT','Deep flat-bottomed eclipses recur in S43,S70,S71 at37.921288 d; approximately8ppt shallower events recur at a distinct phase. These are true eclipses, not heartbeat minima. Gaia37.979418 plus/minus0.049089 d differs by1.18 formal errors. Deep and shallow conjunction offsets are approximately1.1-1.7 local covariance sigma. Independent reduction and image place the deficit at the target.','Capable unresolved neighbors remain a source-ownership limitation; no precision eccentric orbit is claimed.','Resolve neighboring sources and fit both eclipse kinds with RVs.'),
'233624506':('C','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_CONSISTENT','Deep approximately117ppt V-shaped eclipses recur from S14 through S86 on29.006333 d. Shallower approximately40ppt events recur at phase0.5704 after the deep events. The two kinds support noncircular geometry if co-spatial. Gaia28.998850 plus/minus0.008708 d and both source-specific conjunctions agree. Independent custom extraction and difference image recover target-centered loss.','No concrete capable catalogued neighbor found within60arcsec; the2.4arcsec neighbor would require about81.75 intrinsic fractional loss under the idealized flux approximation. Bandpass and throughput remain approximate and arbitrarily close companions cannot be excluded. S86 has a strong baseline discontinuity and is locally fitted.','Resolve neighboring sources and obtain additional RV and two-kind timings.'),
'16150832':('PLAUSIBLE','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_UNTESTED','The S21 raw series contains a sparse shallow cluster near1896.91 BTJD with recovery. It does not provide a usable timing fit or a measured recurrence period. Current TESScut availability returns only S21, matching the sole QLP sector; no later repeat is available.','Single low-amplitude sparse event; morphology, source attribution and Gaia association remain unestablished. This is a completed bounded review with a plausible outcome, not a counted repeated system.','Obtain a new event with source-resolved photometry.')}
rows=[]
for r in q:
 t=r['tic'];v,a,reason,lim,nxt=notes[t];g=gg[t];ev=json.loads((b/t/'lead-timing.json').read_text());c=cl.get(t);p=b/t/'REPORT.md'
 lines=[f"# {r['sample_id']}: TIC {t}",f'Physical verdict: {v}. Full review completion: COMPLETE_BOUNDED. Association: {a}.',reason,'## Identity and raw observations',f"Exact Gaia DR3 {r['gaia_dr3']}, nested G={r['gaia_G']}. ../identity-audit.json verifies source population, TIC FITS headers, sector IDs and SHA256 values. Parent is fresh-band-next1000. Raw mask: finite TIME, positive finite SAP_FLUX and QUALITY=0. Lead independently inspected full-sector and deciding local raw plots.",'| Sector | Center BTJD | Depth ppt | Usable timing |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for e in ev:lines.append(f"| {e['sector']} | {e.get('center_btjd',0):.6f} | {e.get('depth_ppt',0):.2f} | {e.get('fit_usable',False)} |")
 if c:
  lines +=['## Clock and aliases',f"Conditional same-kind recurrence={c['period_d']:.9f} d; formal local period error={c['formal_period_error_d']:.9g} d. Cycle integers={c['cycles']}; residuals(d)={c['residuals']}. Timing floor=max(cadence/2,0.002d); covariance precision is conditional on eclipse kind and cycle selection. Boundary or singular fits are excluded. Distinct depths/conjunction kinds were separated before fitting.",'../lead-alias-covered-windows.json tests measured period, divisors2-6, doubling and Gaia period with actual quality-zero coverage. Core coverage>=75%, no large core gap and both sidebands are required. Missing data and flagged predictions are not nulls. A null requires depth+4*local point scatter < half the characteristic eclipse depth, deliberately conservative in variable/noisy sectors. Timing compatibility must also pass; a doubling cannot explain odd same-kind events merely by having no null. No exhaustive orbital posterior is claimed.','| Trial | Period d | Timing compatible | Covered | Clean nulls |','|---|---:|---|---:|---:|']
  for z in aa[t]:lines.append(f"| {z['label']} | {z['period_d']:.8f} | {z['timing_compatible']} | {z['covered']} | {len(z['nulls'])} |")
 lines+=['## Independent reduction and ownership','helper-localization.json/png and HELPER-AUDIT.md record a fresh TESScut custom aperture, deficit image and neighbor investigation. S7/S33 are separate occasions for Z011; SAP/KSPSAP/custom extraction of one occasion reuse the same photons. Positive neighboring deficit is interpreted physically, not automatically assigned to the target. Unavailable cone queries remain unknown, not nonmatches.','## Gaia geometry',f"Source-specific P={g['gaia_period_d']:.9f} plus/minus{g['gaia_period_error_d']:.8g} d, e={g['eccentricity']:.6f}, omega={g['omega_deg']:.4f} degrees, Tp={g['tp_btjd']:.6f} BTJD; mass function={g['mass_function_solar']:.6g} solar masses. ../lead-gaia-covariance.json uses edge-on conjunctions and the relevant full P,e,omega,Tp correlation submatrix. Fixed-cycle local linear propagation is not a full nonlinear posterior; period equality alone does not prove association. A single event supplies no independent geometry confirmation.",'## Catalogue status','The root-owned sealed ../shared-catalogues receipts provide bounded exact/source-specific matches. Physical tier is separate from novelty and claim eligibility. Known eclipsing identifications exclude novelty; failed queries remain unknown. Z009 was excluded before this exact seven-row queue and was not replaced.','## Limits and next check',lim,nxt,'## Evidence','lead-context.json; lead-series.json; lead-timing.json; lead-fullsectors.png; lead-raw-context.png where flagged; helper artifacts; ../lead-clocks.json; ../lead-alias-covered-windows.json; ../identity-audit.json; ../SOURCE-MANIFEST.json.']
 p.write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf8');rows.append(dict(sample_id=r['sample_id'],tic=t,gaia_dr3=r['gaia_dr3'],physical_verdict=v,full_review_completion='COMPLETE_BOUNDED',period_days=f"{c['period_d']:.9f}" if c else '',period_interpretation='conditional aperture eclipse recurrence' if c else 'not measured',association=a,limitations=lim,next_check=nxt,report=str(p)))
with (b/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf8') as f:w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=rows[0]);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
print('wrote',len(rows))

